These are all networks.

They show the adress of my computer on their own ip book.

For example on docker network, my computer has address `172.17.0.1`.

And what is interesting us is the wireless network `wlp6s0`, where my address is `192.168.1.20`.

But what is the `/24` ?

This is a mask applied to the ip adress range format for this network, meaning that the 24 first bits are set to `1`.

An IPV4 adress is 4 bytes, one byte can represent 256 states -> 0 to 255, that is why IPV4 has this format:

```
[0, 255]:[0, 255]:[0, 255]:[0, 255]
```

In tis case masking the first 24 bits is like masking the 3 first bytes, in consequences it set them to `255`, because underlying bits are `11111111`.

So we got only 256 possibles computers, phones... connected on the local network.

Also, a mask value can be anywhere between 0 and 32, meaning that in IPV4 the bytes are not uncuttable.

So here on my phone i just type the address `http://192.168.1.20:8080` and uploads a bunch of picures of me with interogating face.

